// Two ways to make every developer get the sf-standards plugin. Examples only; nothing here is active.

// 1. One repository: add this to that repository's .devin/config.json.
//    Everyone who opens the repository gets the plugin. Pin a commit sha so updates go through review.
{
  "requiredPlugins": [
    { "source": "git-subdir", "url": "https://github.com/COG-GTM/USAF-tron-common-api.git",
      "path": "demo-basics/plugin/sf-standards", "sha": "<commit sha>" }
  ]
}

// 2. Every repository in the organization: in the Devin web app, an admin opens Customize (sidebar)
//    -> Plugins tab -> Organization (or Enterprise) scope -> Plugin settings (gear) -> Edit manifest,
//    and adds the same entry to "requiredPlugins". Installing from Browse marketplace at that scope does the same.
//    The Organization and Enterprise scope tabs only appear for users with org or enterprise settings access.
//    A repository or a developer cannot remove a plugin required there.
